@@ -206,9 +206,7 @@ Added with the very nice help of GPT-5.3-Codex thanks.
 
 #### Advisor reworks
 
-For the technology advisor in particular, players can now tune as they prefer the tech tree's width. Visual comparison at [Customizable technology advisor width](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Tech_Tree.md#customizable-technology-advisor-width). Also helps not having to open/exit said advisor such as in the technology advisor, where the rival's research and rank position is as of now visible, allowing to better plan tech path without tedium or less of it. Notably, it also features the new "Remove Jungle" and "Chop Down a Forest" buttons (from the Middle-Earth mod thanks!).
-
-Also refactored to make the display more dynamic so that if the advisor's screen dimensions are changed in their respective python file, the rest of the info follows instead of staying stuck at old position which would be weirdly displayed, or so it is easier to change an advisor's screen dimensions if desired later, plus doing some performance optimizations or such i found relevant.
+We notably refactored to make the display more dynamic so that if the advisor's screen dimensions are changed in their respective python file, the rest of the info follows instead of staying stuck at old position which would be weirdly displayed, or so it is easier to change an advisor's screen dimensions if desired later, plus doing some performance optimizations or such i found relevant.
 
 We notably also renamed the Foreign Advisor's Active tab to the "Treaties" tab, removing the redundant bonuses information and beautifying it with icons, and more generally reorganized tabs (for example moving the espionage screen to now being a tab of the foreign advisor (plus beautified and upscaled to screen resolution the espionage tab).

diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index 94c8608ef..d5d26ef61 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -337,7 +337,7 @@ Note: New panels added or modified mostly not mentioned here for concision. See
 - **Main Interface (City Screen)**: Enhanced with a new **Great Person +n ICON** information in relevant Buildings' rows; added a new **Specialists Breakdown** and **Culture Breakdown**; added **optional extra rows** in the **Production Chooser Bar** and **optionally hide the unit bar** (`"PlotListPanel"`) (note: does not affect the production chooser outside of the city screen); added **Buttons** (i.e. icons) in the **Production Queue**; fixed some hard anchored items that now **dynamically** adjust to sides' width. **Beautified** it as well: removed the 3 gray bars ("Trade Routes", "Buildings", "Specialists"), increased sides' width, made bonuses columns even in width, and other changes. These changes allow to now display more information and reduce the need for scrolling or hovering. Also **enlarged** the **Bottom-Left** and **Bottom-Right** panels so they align dynamically with the enlarged **Side Panels**. Enhanced the **city bar** and **other bars**, e.g., `Lakamha: 16 - 12372 (4500BC)` or `Growing - 30/43 (4 Turns)`. Split the **Draft group** into hurry controls on the right (and a **new draft button**) and config options on the right. Add building list filtering buttons ("Show All Buildings", "Show Regular Buildings Only", "Show National Wonders Only", "Show World Wonders Only"). And other changes. Change in [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). See also [KI#101](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#101---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-gp-bar-tooltip-in-city-screen-not-showing-gp-from-obsolete-buildings-yet-seemignly-counting-them-for-the-total-gp-calculation).
 - **Main Interface (Map View)**: **Reordered buttons** (end turn, city change arrows) and wrapped them in a **pretty panel**. Added buttons to unit stack, selected unit. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5503+) Make **left-click on GP bar** open the **corresponding city's city screen**.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5507+) **Main Interface (civilization flag):** **Removed the civilization flag** from the production buttons bar (next to minimap) to show more buttons instead and have a more efficient display. Instead, added **optional compact top-left civilization flag** (with same preserved BtS hover/click behavior) (if **enabled**, left **top text spacing is shifted to make room for the compact flag**). Unlike base AdvCiv, this **optional flag** is **also visible in city screen** because it does not interfere with bottom city-action buttons. This flag is useful to know player civ, hover for player traits, and click to capital's city screen. Default disabled (tunable) as it can be distracting and undesired.
-- Similarly Beautified and Enhanced the **Technology Advisor** in [CvTechChooser.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechChooser.py) so it uses more of the screen while still preserving key information. Players can **tune the advisor's width (4 different options)** in [GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml](/Assets/XML/GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml). See [Customizable technology advisor width](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Tech_Tree.md#customizable-technology-advisor-width).
+- Similarly Beautified and Enhanced the **Technology Advisor** in [CvTechChooser.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvTechChooser.py) so it uses more of the screen while still preserving key information. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5519+) Players can **optionally** set a **lower right space for scoreboard** on **lower game resolutions** (e.g., 1920*1080) so that an **extra column or more is visible** in the technology advisor.
 - **Inverted BUG Options** for the **Technology Advisor** and the **Religion Advisor** so they are more accessible. They are now **enabled as a default**, and ticking their box disables them. Rewrote their text for clarity (e.g. "GP Research" -> **"Hide bulbing indicators"**). See [Inverted BUG options](/README.md#inverted-bug-options).
 
 ### General changes

